{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8f65c9adb2d6597ae569fcfe4abf70e7be0b40f31a640dd64c5f11791360ec72","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion close transition","key_entities":["transition_close.py","verify_completion","head_sha()","rebar transition","require_completion_verification_for_close","completion attestation","--ref","--force-close","reverify-completion"],"problem_keywords":["TOCTOU race","completion verification","race condition","attestation","unsigned closure","HEAD drift","concurrent commit"],"propositions":["A concurrent commit landing between verify and sign steps causes the ticket to close without a completion signature because verify and sign each independently resolve HEAD to different commits.","The current close logic proceeds with the state transition regardless of verify-sign drift, leaving the ticket permanently closed but unsigned with no non-force recovery path.","The verify step must pin a single revision for the entire verify-sign-close unit so that an unrelated HEAD movement cannot invalidate a successful verification of that pinned revision.","A non-force, non-fabrication recovery mechanism is needed for tickets already closed without a completion attestation (e.g. reverify-completion subcommand analogous to resign_plan_review)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787475008405863001,"uuid":"c73b5e3a-c885-490d-9ef1-a04a91fe3312"}